{"id": "EUVD-2026-103814", "enisaUuid": "9f5cacc6-0eb1-3528-b017-a4bdf402d3cf", "description": "In the Linux kernel, the following vulnerability has been resolved:\n\nx86/mm: Don't apply va_align to hugetlb mappings on AMD F15h\n\nget_align_mask() returns huge_page_mask_align() for hugetlbfs, but get_align_bits()\nadds va_align.bits regardless, so vm_unmapped_area() returns an address off the huge\npage boundary and __unmap_hugepage_range() hits BUG_ON(start & ~huge_page_mask(h)) at\nteardown.\n\nThis can be triggered on Carrizo and FX-8370E, both hstates.\n\nPass the file to get_align_bits() and skip the randomisation for hugetlbfs.\n\n  [ bp: Massage commit message. ]", "datePublished": "2026-10-18T15:47:06", "dateUpdated": "2026-10-19T09:24:39", "baseScore": 0.0, "references": ["https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/fe23680e6f1d52b8cc45d77bf7c54249508a81c7", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/b46b2e2de47ca9449532b0a7110ed99f79061d6e", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/d2457a7e2727dc747a61a50d65c2f259afce8c45"], "aliases": ["CVE-2026-98729", "GHSA-c8p2-ffwx-rgc9"], "assigner": "Linux", "epss": 0.17, "enisaIdProduct": [{"id": "1223c904-07a8-37e1-b24f-b2af7e14fc68", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 0"}, {"id": "260fb0fe-30a0-38c9-8a9f-941768176a5e", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 7.2.10"}, {"id": "56459f40-6cfa-300c-8cd4-6a5ba5b1c995", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "1317a5e7f7b1336eac4097f0ef4f5cd7ae72f1d0 <d2457a7e2727dc747a61a50d65c2f259afce8c45"}, {"id": "5c023202-3861-3602-9bd1-75910632a13c", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "1317a5e7f7b1336eac4097f0ef4f5cd7ae72f1d0 <b46b2e2de47ca9449532b0a7110ed99f79061d6e"}, {"id": "66273b2a-3ad2-38d3-bae5-f1913ace5f32", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "1317a5e7f7b1336eac4097f0ef4f5cd7ae72f1d0